{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"coupled pressure velocity and temperature fields coupled pressure velocity and temperature fields","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md","fileName":"Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"coupled pressure velocity and temperature fields coupled pressure velocity and temperature fields","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md","fileName":"Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields","heading":"Coupled Pressure Velocity and Temperature Fields","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Fluid pressure and velocity satisfy mass and momentum conservation, while temperature satisfies energy conservation. In a nonisothermal model, advection carries thermal energy and temperature-dependent properties feed back into the momentum equations.\n\nBoundary conditions must be compatible across all three fields: an inlet may specify flow and temperature, an outlet may constrain pressure, and walls impo